    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p15_b2",
      "text": "All experiments were conducted on a single server equipped with eight NVIDIA A800-SXM4-80GB GPUs. To ensure\ncomputational efficiency and minimize resource requirements, we pre-computed and cached the outputs of the reference\nmodel before starting our main training runs. This strategy allows both our LBR and LBP methods to train with VRAM\nusage nearly identical to that of the baseline, incurring negligible memory overhead and only a minor increase in training\ntime.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.08,
        88.05,
        541.44,
        145.9
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        352,
        2165,
        583
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 468,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p15_b3",
      "text": "LBR Implementation.\nFor the Visual Instruction Tuning stage with LBR, we followed the official training procedure of\nLLaVA. Training the 7B model required 4 GPUs and took approximately 30 hours, while the 13B model utilized 8 GPUs\nand took about 36 hours. Given that our setup closely mirrors the standard LLaVA training, we omit a detailed reiteration of\ncommon hyperparameters.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.44,
        160.96,
        541.44,
        206.86
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        221,
        643,
        2165,
        827
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.95,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 379,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p15_b4",
      "text": "LBP Implementation.\nFor the Direct Preference Optimization stage with LBP, all experiments were conducted using\n4 GPUs. On the RLHF-V dataset, fine-tuning the LLaVA-v1.5-7B model for 3 epochs took approximately 1.4 hours.\nFine-tuning the LLaVA-v1.5-13B model for 4 epochs required about 2.6 hours. Training times on the larger VLFeedback\ndataset scale proportionally with the data size. A comprehensive list of all hyperparameters for LBP is provided in Table 10.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.09,
        221.83,
        543.19,
        267.8
